/ snapshot: a run's exact state, saved to a file or a store and gone on with later, even after its program changed or
/ the program moved where it goes on. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each comment a behaviour we want,
/ and the step under it runs the plang test that proves it; a behaviour proved only in C# names its test. The text is
/ start.md.
Start
- call Save
- call Resume
- call Edit

Save
/ save snapshot answers the run's state as a value: its variables and its call stack, the frame it runs in by its goal's
/ path, kept in a .plang file signed and read back
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/save/SavesTheRun
/ a plain value is saved as its token, one whose token can't say its type keeps it — C# test SignedSnapshotTests
/ (ASavedRow_SaysItsType_OnlyWhereItsTokenCant); a [Sensitive] value is never saved — C# test SignedSnapshotTests
/ (ASensitiveLeaf_ComesBackNull)

Resume
/ a run saved inside a goal it called, kept in a file and resumed, goes on from its save in an app of its own: the
/ called goal finishes, its caller goes on after the call, and nothing before the save runs again
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/resume/FreshAppGoesOn
/ a call saved mid-step is finished, then the rest of its step runs once — never the call again — C# test
/ SnapshotResumeTests (SnapshotResume_InsideACall_FinishesIt_ThenTheRestOfTheCallingStep_Once)
/ a run saved inside a bound call keeps %!event%: resumed, it reads what the event fired for
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/resume/EventComesBack
/ a goal changed since the save is the goal as it is now: the run goes on at its saved place, and another action
/ standing there is said on the error channel — C# tests CallSnapshotTests
/ (Call_Resume_AStepInsertedWhereTheRunStopped_RunsIt_ThenTheStepItStoppedIn, Call_Resume_AnotherActionAtThePlace_GoesOnThere_AndSaysSo)
/ a resume's app is a sub app of the resuming actor: a binding the resuming app made, which the snapshot never held,
/ fires in the resumed run
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/resume/ResumeTakesInTheBinding
/ a sub app's save holds only what it bound itself — C# test SavedBindingsTests (ASubAppsSave_HoldsItsBindingsOnly)
/ a resume goes on only from a snapshot one of this app's identities signed, as it is — C# test SignedSnapshotTests

Edit
/ where a run goes on is two numbers, each its frame's own: a program moves them, signs the snapshot again, and the run
/ goes on there
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/resume/EditedStopPoint
/ an edit changes the snapshot alone: the program that runs keeps its steps' places, and a step's own place is no
/ program's to write
- call /plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/resume/EditLeavesTheProgram
/ an edit no one signed again is refused — C# test SignedSnapshotTests (AnEditedSnapshot_NotSignedAgain_IsRefused); an
/ edited snapshot kept again is the saved bytes plus the edit — C# test SignedSnapshotTests
/ (AnEditedSnapshot_KeptAgain_IsTheSavedBytes_PlusTheEdit)
